# Ranked Fitness rules

## Design (Nocturne)

- Use design tokens from `src/theme/tokens.ts` only — never hardcode colors, radii, or shadows.
- Accent is for lines, outlines, and glows only. Never fill large areas with accent.
- Buttons are outlined (1px accent border on transparent), never solid-filled. Use `OutlineButton`.
- Typography is Inter, max weight 500 for headings. Hierarchy comes from size and space, never bolder weights.
- Icons are Phosphor (regular weight; fill variant for active/completed states).
- No pure black or white anywhere.

## Architecture

- All data access goes through `src/services/DataService.ts` (`IDataService`). Screens never own data logic; the Zustand store (`src/store/useAppStore.ts`) delegates to the service.
- Challenge tunables live in `src/constants/challenge.ts` (XP, ping quota, challenge length) and `src/constants/tiers.ts` (tier task sets and missed-day penalties). Never hardcode task counts — every "X of N" derives from the active tier's task array.
- Keep `EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK` working; the mock DataService is the only implementation until the backend exists.
- Gestures run through `react-native-gesture-handler` with animations driven by `react-native-reanimated` on the UI thread.
- The hidden dev menu (600ms long-press on the RANKED wordmark) must stay functional in dev builds for QA of scenarios, tiers, solo mode, and screen states.
